1
00:00:00,390 --> 00:00:02,990
When it comes to technology, we love to

2
00:00:02,990 --> 00:00:04,990
split people into two categories.

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:09,350
The first is digital natives and the second

4
00:00:09,350 --> 00:00:10,970
is digital immigrants.

5
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:16,430
One group grew up with screens, the other

6
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:18,730
had to learn the language a bit late,

7
00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:20,950
or in some cases very late.

8
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:24,510
But the whole story might be wrong.

9
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:26,770
The picture is simple.

10
00:00:27,770 --> 00:00:32,390
If we are born after the internet, you

11
00:00:32,390 --> 00:00:33,510
just get technology.

12
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:37,210
Sometimes you may even think it's your mother

13
00:00:37,210 --> 00:00:37,610
tongue.

14
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:46,910
And if you were born before technology, sometimes

15
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:50,230
we may feel accents when you use these

16
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:50,790
technologies.

17
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:54,890
And in some cases, you may even fumble

18
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:57,590
and require your children to help you with

19
00:00:57,590 --> 00:00:58,410
some of the settings.

20
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:01,930
Here is what we miss in the story.

21
00:01:02,990 --> 00:01:06,850
Being a native speaker has never made anyone

22
00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:07,590
a good writer.

23
00:01:09,810 --> 00:01:11,690
And growing up with phones in your hands

24
00:01:11,690 --> 00:01:14,450
does not make you wise about what is

25
00:01:14,450 --> 00:01:14,970
on the screen.

26
00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:18,670
Researchers have a simple way of putting it.

27
00:01:20,310 --> 00:01:23,470
A digital native can also be a digital

28
00:01:23,470 --> 00:01:24,010
naive.

29
00:01:25,430 --> 00:01:28,110
They can swipe faster than anyone alive.

30
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:32,470
Things will begin to fall apart when you

31
00:01:32,470 --> 00:01:35,690
ask them to explain what they just read.

32
00:01:36,650 --> 00:01:41,190
Ask them who is collecting their data and

33
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:41,910
what is the what.

34
00:01:43,270 --> 00:01:45,530
Ask them why the app costs them nothing.

35
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:50,900
And very often, there is no answer.

36
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,600
Fluency is not the same as understanding.

37
00:01:56,740 --> 00:02:00,080
You can be born inside a house and

38
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:02,540
still have no idea how it is built

39
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:05,460
or who is holding the key.

40
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:11,060
So maybe the real divide is never about

41
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:11,520
age.

42
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:15,780
It is not about native versus immigrants.

43
00:02:17,970 --> 00:02:21,030
It is the people who question the screen

44
00:02:21,030 --> 00:02:24,350
and the people who simply trust it.

45
00:02:25,490 --> 00:02:27,570
So which one are you?

46
00:02:28,570 --> 00:02:32,110
Not by the year you were born, but

47
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:33,010
by the way you think.

48
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:35,990
Follow for more.
